nter\"><b>60.0%</b>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:75px;text-align:center\">37.0%\n</td></tr>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n</tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr /><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas_results_map_by_county.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas_results_map_by_county.svg/330px-2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"300\" height=\"157\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas_results_map_by_county.svg/960px-2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas_results_map_by_county.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"810\" data-file-height=\"424\" /></a></span><div>County results<br /><b>Moran:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#e27f7f; color:#e27f7f;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;50–60%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d75d5d; color:#d75d5d;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#d72f30; color:#d72f30;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;70–80%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#c21b18; color:#c21b18;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;80–90%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#a80000; color:#a80000;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;&gt;90%</span><br /><b>Holland:</b> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#a5b0ff; color:#a5b0ff;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;40–50%</span> <span style=\"margin:0px; font-size:90%;\"><span style=\"border:none; background-color:#6674de; color:#6674de;\">&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</span>&#160;60–70%</span></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-full-data\"><hr />\n<table role=\"presentation\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:transparent; color: inherit; width:100%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:left;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Kansas\" title=\"List of United States senators from Kansas\">U.S. senator</a> before election</b><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Jerry_Moran\" title=\"Jerry Moran\">Jerry Moran</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"width:50%; text-align:right;\"><b>Elected U.S. Senator</b> <br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/Jerry_Moran\" title=\"Jerry Moran\">Jerry Moran</a><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas\" title=\"2022 United States Senate election in Kansas\">2022 United States Senate election in Kansas</a></div>\n<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" /><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">See also: <a href=\"/wiki/List_of_United_States_senators_from_Kansas\" title=\"List of United States senators from Kansas\">List of United States senators from Kansas</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/2022_United_States_House_of_Representatives_elections_in_Kansas\" title=\"2022 United States House of Representatives elections in Kansas\">2022 United States House of Representatives elections in Kansas</a></div>\n<p>Two-term Republican <a href=\"/wiki/Jerry_Moran\" title=\"Jerry Moran\">Jerry Moran</a> was <a href=\"/wiki/2016_United_States_Senate_election_in_Kansas\" title=\"2016 United States Senate election in Kansas\">re-elected in 2016</a> with 62.2% of the vote. He announced that he was seeking re-election in 2020.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-auto1&#95;160-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-auto1-160\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>135<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Democratic <a href=\"/wiki/United_Methodist\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"United Methodist\">United Methodist</a> pastor and former <a href=\"/wiki/Kansas_City,_Kansas\" title=\"Kansas City, Kansas\">Kansas City</a> mayor <a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Holland_(American_politician)\" title=\"Mark Holland (American politician)\">Mark Holland</a> challenged Moran.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-KSHB&#95;161-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-KSHB-161\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>136<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\";\">\n<caption>Kansas Republican primary<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-KSprimary&#95;162-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-KSprimary-162\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>137<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th scope=\"col\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"width: 15em\">Party\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 17em\">Candidate\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 5em\">Votes\n</th>\n<th scope=\"col\" style=\"width: 3.5em\">%\n</th></tr>\n\n\n<tr class=\"vcard\">\n<td style=\"color:inherit;background-color:#E81B23;width:5px\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"org\" style=\"width:130px\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)\" title=\"Republican Party (United States)\">Republican</a></b>\n</td>\n<th scope=\"row\" st